# Build-context exclusions for every image built from this repo root
# (Dockerfile, server/design-agent/Dockerfile).
#
# The load-bearing entry is `.venv` — server/design-agent/Dockerfile creates
# the Design Agent's Python venv itself (`python3 -m venv
# server/design-agent/python/.venv`) and then runs `COPY server ./server`
# AFTERWARDS. Without this file, a developer's local .venv present in the
# build context is copied straight over the one the image just built. That
# venv's `bin/python3` is a macOS binary (and a different Python minor
# version — 3.14 locally vs the image's 3.12), so the copied interpreter is
# not executable under Linux: every design_generate job then dies at spawn
# with ENOENT before Python ever starts. Keep this entry even if the venv is
# also gitignored — .gitignore governs git, not the Docker build context, so
# any build run from a working tree that has one (a dev machine, or a CI
# runner that installed it) would silently ship a broken image.
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Never ship dependency trees or build output — the images install/build
# their own (`npm ci`, `pip install`, `vite build`). Copying these in is
# both wrong (host-platform native modules) and enormous.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
dist/

# Secrets must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Repo/tooling noise with no runtime meaning.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
